    "label": "61",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n$$\\frac{3x^6y^4}{6x^2y^7}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{x^4}{2y^3}$, $x,y\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3x^6y^4}{6x^2y^7}&=\\frac12x^{6-2}y^{4-7}\\\\\\frac{3x^6y^4}{6x^2y^7}&=\\frac12x^4y^{-3}\\\\\\frac{3x^6y^4}{6x^2y^7}&=\\frac{x^4}{2y^3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominator requires $x,y\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
